# MBZ-2140 Angular 14 -> 15 deprecation / changed-pattern log (northgate-business-web)
# Source: the per-step logs in this directory (A1-node16/, A2-rxjs7/, A3-angular-eslint14/, A4-canopy-3.7.2/,
# B-canopy-4.0.0/, C-angular15/). One block per ordered step; every pattern that was rewritten is listed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A1  Node 14.21.3 -> 16.20.2 / npm 6.14.18 -> 8.19.4  (commit 6d574ef, MBZ-2231)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   - .nvmrc, package.json engines, Dockerfile FROM node:16.20.2-bullseye-slim, Jenkinsfile agentLabel nodejs16-rhel8 /
#     nodeVersion '16.20.2'; the CHROME_BIN override (/opt/google/chrome-109/chrome, rhel7 image) is removed because the
#     nodejs16-rhel8 image ships Chrome 120 and the shared library default points at it.
#   - package-lock.json v1 -> v2 (npm 8 "old lockfile" one-time fix-up, A1-node16/npm-install-lockfile.log). Angular 14
#     resolutions kept; a fresh resolve was rejected by engine-strict (transitive node-releases@2.0.54/55 declares
#     engines node>=18, which npm 8 enforces on transitive packages and npm 6 did not).
#   - package.json "overrides": { "node-releases": "2.0.44" } + direct devDependency node-releases 2.0.6 -> 2.0.44
#     (last release without an engines field). This is an engines/resolution override, NOT an audit override:
#     node-releases has no advisory at any version. Disclosed for the GIS .npmrc/CODEOWNERS review under KAN-29.
#   - .npmrc: engine-strict=true and save-exact=true kept; comment text updated to the Node 16 pin. legacy-peer-deps
#     kept until A2.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A2  RxJS 6.6.7 -> 7.5.7  (commit 4e8f9e0, MBZ-2044 pattern list)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   - Observable#toPromise() (deprecated in 7, removed in 8) -> lastValueFrom(obs) in 49 call sites across 21 files;
#     per-line list in A2-rxjs7/toPromise-migration.log. lastValueFrom (not firstValueFrom) was chosen everywhere
#     because toPromise() resolved with the LAST emitted value; every call site is a single-shot HttpClient / of()
#     stream so the two are equivalent, and lastValueFrom preserves the 6.x semantics exactly. Behaviour difference
#     kept in mind: toPromise() resolved undefined on an empty completion, lastValueFrom rejects with EmptyError.
#     No call site consumes an empty stream (all are HTTP responses or of(...)); no spec needed a change.
#     Two of the 21 files are in the frozen legacy module (src/app/legacy/audit-log/legacy-audit-log.component.ts,
#     src/app/legacy/statements/legacy-statements.component.ts, one call each): the same mechanical rewrite, no other
#     edit, still excluded from lint (ignorePatterns). Recorded because ADR 0003 calls the module frozen.
#   - `import { lastValueFrom } from 'rxjs'` added to each touched file; no `rxjs/operators` import had to move
#     (the repo already imported operators from 'rxjs/operators', which remains valid in 7.5; the 'rxjs' root export
#     of operators is not adopted here to keep the diff to the toPromise change).
#   - No rxjs-compat, no `rxjs/Rx`, no `rxjs/internal/*` imports existed (baseline tslint import-blacklist).
#   - Subscription / Subscriber typing: no changes needed (no `Subscription.add(...)` return-value use, no
#     `subscribe(next, error, complete)` positional-argument form in src/; legacy module included).
#   - .npmrc legacy-peer-deps=true REMOVED: npm install without it resolves with 0 ERESOLVE
#     (A2-rxjs7/legacy-peer-deps-check.log). codelyzer 6.0.2 still nested its own @angular/core 9 peer as before;
#     gone in A3.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A3  TSLint 6.1.3 + codelyzer 6.0.2 -> angular-eslint 14.4.0 / eslint 8.57.1 / @typescript-eslint 5.43.0  (d00f527)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   - tslint.json deleted; .eslintrc.json created by `ng g @angular-eslint/schematics:convert-tslint-to-eslint`.
#     Rule-by-rule outcome (untranslatable, silently-dropped-and-hand-mapped, re-scoped) in
#     A3-angular-eslint14/rule-conversion-notes.md. Nothing disabled silently; one gap: TSLint `deprecation`
#     (warning) has no equivalent without eslint-plugin-deprecation (not in the approved set) - listed for review.
#   - package.json scripts: "tslint", "tslint:fix" removed; "lint": "ng lint", "lint:fix": "ng lint --fix".
#     Jenkinsfile lintCommand 'npm run tslint' -> 'npm run lint'. angular.json gains the @angular-eslint/builder:lint
#     target and the schematics defaults block.
#   - Code changes forced by the stricter ESLint equivalents (type annotations only, no behaviour change):
#       6 explicit return types (3 closures; 3 NgRx selector factories typed MemoizedSelector<object, T>) in
#       fixture-data.service.ts, telemetry.service.ts, ach.service.ts, shell.component.ts,
#       approvals.reducer.spec.ts, approvals.selectors.ts, entitlements.selectors.ts.
#   - Warning count 88 (tslint) -> 90 (eslint); every warning rule was already warning-severity in tslint.json.
