# A4  @northgate/canopy-ui 3.5.0 -> 3.7.2  (commit 4cec227, MBZ-2210 hop 1; Angular 14 unchanged)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   - Pin only (package.json + lockfile, 28 lines). Canopy 3.6.x token rename / table internals and 3.7.x density
#     mode: business-web already consumed the public Canopy 3.7 surface (CnCoreModule.forRoot({ density: 'compact' })
#     and --cn-* tokens), and the ADR 0004 fear (twenty `::ng-deep` overrides breaking on 3.6) did not materialise:
#     the `::ng-deep` rules that reach into Canopy do so by BEM class name (`.cn-page-shell__nav-badge`,
#     `.cn-page-shell__nav-link`, `.cn-expansion .mat-expansion-panel-header`, `.cn-checkbox__label`) and 3.6/3.7/4.0
#     kept those names; the rest target Material `.mat-*` internals and are dealt with in C. Build, 32/32 tests, lint,
#     0 new audit ids (A4-canopy-3.7.2/gate-summary.txt). `grep ::ng-deep src` gives 12 hits after C (develop: 15;
#     both counts include the comment in styles.scss): eleven rules, six of them into Canopy `.cn-*` class names
#     (two of those six also carry an MDC class) and five into MDC public classes/tokens only; moving the Canopy
#     ones to tokens is follow-up, not this hop.
